From: David J. Vandenburgh <david@vandenburgh.co>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apply the preferred mode to internal screens only

-W, -H and -r give the size and rate of the built-in panel, and
setup_best_connector() looked for that exact mode on whichever display
it picked. On a docked TV that lists the same mode (1920x1080 at 120 Hz
on many current TVs), gamescope pinned it and never reached the mode
Steam saved for that TV in GAMESCOPE_MODE_SAVE_FILE, so the resolution
picked in Steam's display settings was lost on every replug. An
external display now goes straight to its saved mode, then to its own
preferred one.
---
diff --git a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
index b47b329..021c2e3 100644
--- a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
@@ -1444,7 +1444,10 @@ static bool setup_best_connector(struct drm_t *drm, bool force, bool initial)
 	s_ExternalBroadcastRGBMode = GAMESCOPE_BROADCAST_RGB_MODE_AUTOMATIC;
 
 	const drmModeModeInfo *mode = nullptr;
-	if ( drm->preferred_width != 0 || drm->preferred_height != 0 || drm->preferred_refresh != 0 )
+	// -W/-H/-r describe the built-in panel. Applied to an external display they would pin a TV
+	// that happens to list that mode and skip the mode Steam saved for it below.
+	if ( best->GetScreenType() == gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_INTERNAL &&
+		( drm->preferred_width != 0 || drm->preferred_height != 0 || drm->preferred_refresh != 0 ) )
 	{
 		mode = find_mode(best->GetModeConnector(), drm->preferred_width, drm->preferred_height, gamescope::ConvertmHzToHz( drm->preferred_refresh ));
 	}
